index 0000000..9c85bd0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/legacy-origin/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+# Old-origin files (https://www.dailygrind.coffee)
+
+The Daily Grind installed app moves from `https://www.dailygrind.coffee` to
+`https://order.dailygrind.coffee`. The two origins are same-site (`dailygrind.coffee`),
+which Web App Origin Migration requires.
+
+The files in this folder are **not** served by this repo. Deploy them to the root of the **old** origin:
+
+| File | Purpose |
+| --- | --- |
+| `.well-known/web-app-origin-association` | The old origin allows the new origin to take over the installation. Serve as `application/json`. |
+| `manifest.webmanifest` | Replaces the old manifest. `migrate_to` asks the browser to start migrating existing installs now. |
+| `migration-bridge.html` | Gives saved `dailygrind.*` localStorage settings to the new origin (data is not migrated automatically). Send `Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors https://order.dailygrind.coffee`. |
+| `migration-banner.js` | Fallback banner for browsers without origin migration (Firefox, Safari). Add it to every old page. |
+
+On the new origin (repo root), `manifest.webmanifest` declares `migrate_from`, and
+`migrate-settings.js` imports the settings once on first launch.
+
+To make the upgrade mandatory rather than suggested, add `"behavior": "force"` to the
+`migrate_from` entry in the new manifest. The browser then asks the user to either update or remove the app.
